# .env.example — every knob the launcher reads, what it does, and what it costs.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is `.`-sourced by local-start.sh, so `$HOME`
# and `${VAR}` expand; keep single quotes on JSON values (bash strips bare
# double quotes and the container's json.loads then fails).
#
# Values below are the config that produced the numbers in README.md on
# 4x RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB + 128 GB RAM. Different hardware means re-deriving the
# VRAM-coupled knobs — each entry says which ones.

# ─── paths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the checkpoint lives. Must contain model.safetensors.index.json.
# Get it per docs/RUNNING.md step 2 (Intel AutoRound W4A16 target + FP8 PLE assembly).
MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-FP8PLE

# Root for host-side assets (PLE tables, KV tier, grafts). docker_serve.sh derives
# MODELS_DIR / PLEQUANT_DIR from this; set them explicitly to put assets on
# separate disks.
LANE_HOME=$HOME
MODELS_DIR=$LANE_HOME/models
PLEQUANT_DIR=$LANE_HOME/plequant

# Out-of-tree vLLM overlays, bind-mounted read-only over the installed package.
# Tree layout = path relative to the `vllm` python package. Unset = pure image
# behaviour (you lose the hybrid tier, the GDN prefill kernel and the all-reduce win).
# Everything needed to boot is here. One optional file — the FlashInfer GDN prefill gate
# for SM12x — is NOT included because its source recipe publishes no license: see
# README §1a for where to pull it and what to do if you skip it (skipping is safe).
FN_EXT_DIR=$HOME/qwen38-flash-next/fn-ext

# ─── topology ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8000
# Tensor-parallel size. This repo's tuning is TP4 + expert-parallel; TP2 also
# works (2x24 GB cards is the upstream target) and allows a different all-reduce posture.
TP_SIZE=4
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3

# ─── the expert tier (this repo's reason to exist) ───────────────────────────
# Which mechanism decides what expert bytes live in VRAM. Cold boot to change.
#   0 = mirror + dynamic LRU        decode-first (this box: 55.4 tok/s, 1258 pp@3k)
#   1 = contiguous VMM view only    prefill-first, no mirror (37.6 tok/s, 1670 pp@3k)
#   2 = HYBRID (default here)       both paths on one tier (56.0 tok/s, 1727 pp@3k)
# 2 costs ~+20 GiB pinned host RAM and ~+240 MiB VRAM/card vs 1. See
# docs/hybrid-vmm-lru-mechanism.md before changing it.
PREFILL_VMM_ARM=2

# How many experts per layer per rank stay in VRAM. This competes directly with
# the KV pool for the same bytes (~116 MiB/slot/card here). Measured flat 32-44
# under arm 0; under arm 2 every extra slot removes PCIe miss copies, so this is
# the lever to test next. Too high = boot OOM or pool shrink.
VLLM_WNA16_STATIC_HOT_CACHE_SIZE=44

# Host-side expert pool per rank. Experts don't fit in VRAM, so this is the
# resident host copy: total across ranks ~64 GiB on this box. Must stay below
# physical RAM minus the rest of the working set or you pay swap during decode.
CPU_OFFLOAD_GB=16

# ─── context length and the KV pool ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The pool is sized MANUALLY by KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES: vLLM prints
# "GPU KV cache size: N tokens ... Maximum concurrency: Mx" at boot and that N is
# the only witness that your numbers are consistent. Rule: N >= MAX_MODEL_LEN.
# Bytes/token/card on this model ≈ 13,214 (main QSA K+V + side caches), pool ≈ 1.03-1.05x.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=495000
KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=3635000000
# fp8_e4m3 main KV (needs the QSA overlay pair in fn-ext; without it the overlay
# raises and only auto|bfloat16 boots). fp8 frees ~1 GiB/card but costs ~10%
# decode and full-precision recall certainty — owner trade, both arms are one line.
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8

# Extending past the checkpoint's trained window uses YaRN. Two things are
# required together and the failure modes are different:
#   VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1 - bypasses the validator that still measures
#     the un-extended architecture. It skips the comparison, not the rope math.
#   HF_OVERRIDES_JSON               - actually applies the rope scaling. factor =
#     target / 262144, and max_position_embeddings must be raised too or startup
#     aborts with a pydantic ValidationError.
# Verify it landed: the boot banner's "non-default args" must contain hf_overrides,
# and a needle probe must recall a position past the trained window.
VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1
#HF_OVERRIDES_JSON='{"text_config":{"max_position_embeddings":495000,"rope_parameters":{"rope_type":"yarn","factor":1.888275146484375,"original_max_position_embeddings":262144,"attn_factor":1.0,"beta_fast":32,"beta_slow":1,"mrope_interleaved":true,"mrope_section":[11,11,10],"partial_rotary_factor":0.25,"rope_theta":10000000}},"max_position_embeddings":495000}'

# ─── batching / scheduling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Chunked-prefill budget. It sizes a transient slab ON CARD (~+160 MiB/card per
# +2048). Halving it halves prefill throughput (fixed ~2 s/chunk cost); raising it
# boot-OOMs once the pin budget is at the ceiling. 4096 is both optimum and ceiling here.
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=4096
# Concurrent sequences. batch-2 CUDA-graph capture deadlocks on this hybrid stack
# (upstream #52682 family) unless capture sizes are pinned — see COMPILATION_CONFIG.
MAX_NUM_SEQS=2
# Pin the graph capture set so batch-1 steps stay graphed and mixed batch-2 steps
# run eager. mode 0 = default compile mode; FULL_DECODE_ONLY graphs decode only.
COMPILATION_CONFIG='{"mode":0,"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_DECODE_ONLY","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,2]}'
# Overlap scheduling with GPU work. +6.7% decode measured here, at the price of
# ~+500-800 MiB/card retained per card (the ratchet in nvidia-smi after first traffic).
ASYNC_SCHED=1
# Speculative decoding depth. OFF on bandwidth-pinned lanes: with accept rate ~2.5-2.8
# the arithmetic (tg_off x accept / 4 >= tg) cannot win at depth <= 3.
MTP_DEPTH=0
# Load the multimodal tower. Off = language-model-only (frees VRAM, no image input).
VISION=1
# Limit parallel weight loaders: fewer concurrent readers = lower peak host RAM at boot.
MAX_PARALLEL_LOADING_WORKERS=1

# ─── collectives (multi-GPU latency) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Custom all-reduce: needs the fn-ext overlay for >2 GPUs (upstream refuses PCIe-only
# TP>2). Pairing rule enforced by the launcher: DISABLE_CUSTOM_ALL_REDUCE=0 requires
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False — the pinned runtime cannot combine
# them. ~+7% decode with the overlay, so all three of these move together or none.
DISABLE_CUSTOM_ALL_REDUCE=0
VLLM_CUSTOM_AR_ALLOW_PCIE=1
PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False
# Allow NCCL P2P across the PCIe host bridge (needed on a patched consumer driver;
# without it NCCL may stage through shared memory on the x4 links).
NCCL_P2P_LEVEL=SYS
# With all-reduces on custom AR, the remaining NCCL payload is the ~2 MB logits
# all-gather, where Simple beats LL.
NCCL_PROTO=Simple
# One-shot IPC all-gather for that same logits payload (needs custom AR active;
# >2 MB falls back to NCCL). Measured neutral, kept because it removes a sync point.
VLLM_CUSTOM_ALL_GATHER=1
# QSA exact top-k selection: 0 = approximate (fast, the shipped posture).
# 1 = exact scoring, slower, used only for accuracy experiments.
VLLM_QSA_EXACT_TOPK=0

# ─── PLE (n-gram memory table) tier ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The n-gram table is 47.7 GiB (fp8) or 95.4 GiB (bf16). Serving it from an NVMe
# mmap keeps it out of both the VRAM and the pinned-RAM budget; page cache does
# the rest. Generate the table first — docs/RUNNING.md step 3 — then pick the dtype.
# The table DIRECTORY is derived from the dtype flag; do not set a dir separately
# (a half-toggled pair is a refused-boot, by design).
PLE_ARM_DISK8=1
PLE_BF16_TABLE=1        # 1 = bf16 (95.4 GiB), 0 = fp8 (47.7 GiB)

# Alternative PLE tiers, mutually exclusive with disk8 (they bind-mount the same files):
#   PLE_ARM_INT4=1    primitive-ai packed int4 sidecar (~30 GiB, needs ples_int4 dir)
#   PLE_ARM_NVFP4=1   packed e2m1 sidecar (~28.8 GiB, page-cache regime)
# Both need their graft trees present under PLEQUANT_DIR (or the *_DIR override) and
# the sidecar dir under MODELS_DIR. Int4 costs ~19% decode (CPU row-dequant); the
# packed variant removes that. Default off = the disk8 tier above.
PLE_ARM_INT4=0
PLE_ARM_NVFP4=0
#VLLM_PLE_QUANT_DIR=/ples_nvfp4
#VLLM_PLE_PACKED=1
#PLE_ARM_NVFP4_DIR=$PLEQUANT_DIR/nvfp4/arm
# Time to wait for the 4 PLE offload workers to register at boot.
VLLM_PLE_OFFLOAD_READY_TIMEOUT=1200

# ─── KV disk tier (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overflow KV to disk so a session that exceeds the VRAM pool resumes instead of
# re-prefilling. Use SimpleCPUOffloadConnector (not OffloadingConnector: the group
# assert dies on the QSA scratch group in images predating upstream #54743).
# disk_path is INSIDE the container (the host dir below is mounted there) and must be
# unique per config — KV bytes depend on the PLE/KV dtype, hence the g12-bf16 tag.
# The slot map is in RAM: this cache does NOT survive a lane restart.
# Comment both lines out to disable entirely.
#KV_TIER_DIR=$MODELS_DIR/kv-tier
#KV_TIER_JSON='{"kv_connector":"SimpleCPUOffloadConnector","kv_role":"kv_both","kv_connector_extra_config":{"kv_offload_backend":"disk","disk_path":"/kv_tier/g12-bf16","disk_capacity_bytes":13421772800,"disk_buffer_slots":4}}'

# ─── image / container ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#IMAGE=qwen38-flash-next-2x3090:locked   # built from docker/Dockerfile (see docs/RUNNING.md step 1)
#SERVED_MODEL_NAME=Qwen3.8-Flash-Next    # the name clients send in "model"
